<title>USA: Enron sells 50 pct of Guam power plant.</title>
<headline>Enron sells 50 pct of Guam power plant.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Enron Corp announced Monday it has sold a 50 percent interest in its power project in Piti, Guam to Tomen Corp of Japan.</p>
<p>Terms of the sale were not released.</p>
<p>In September 1996, Enron said it was selected by the Guam government to construct an 80 megawatt (MW) power plant, which is expected to be in operation by December 1998.</p>
<p>Under a build-operate-transfer arrangement, the plant will be transferred to the Guam Power Authority in 20 years.</p>
<p>An Energy Conversion Agreement signed in September 1996 stipulates that the Guam Power Authority will provide the fuel and Enron will convert it to electricity.</p>
</text>
